<h1>More Info</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <b><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Reports &gt;More Info</b></span></b> in <span class="Mode" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Inspection</u></span> <span lang="EN-US">mode or by pressing</span> <b><i style="font-style:normal; font-weight:bold;"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>More Info</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button</span></i> in the Inspection toolbar.</b></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">The</span> <b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Command">More Info</span></b> <span lang="EN-US">function provides you statistical information.</span></p>
<p><img src="../Inspection_Mode_files/more_info.gif" width="479px" height="359px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Enter unit for measurement</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">You can enter custom unit for measurement, different from the default (Standard deviation).</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Recalculate button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">When you click it, in the table on the bottom of this dialog you can see what percentage of points is inside and outside the given value, doubled given value and tripled given value.</span></p>
<p class="sub-head">General section</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Standard deviation</span> -</b> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Sigma - represents the dispersion of the point distance to the reference values around the average of their absolute values. Most of them should be somewhere around one Sigma away from the average. Few will be more than two sigma and very few more than three sigma.</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Minimum</span> - t</b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">he minimum value of a point distance to the reference.</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Maximum</span> - t</b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">he maximum value of a point distance to the reference.</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Average</span> - t</b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">he average of the absolute values of the point distances to the reference.</font></span></p>
<p class="sub-head">Range section</p>
<p><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">The Minimum and Maximum values were defined in the range section of Inspection pane.</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Minimum</font></span></b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">- the lower range border</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Maximum</font></span></b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">- the upper range border</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Inside</font></span></b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">- the percentage of points inside this range</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Outside</font></span></b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">- the percentage of points outside this range</font></span></p>
<p class="sub-head">Zero range section</p>
<p class="whs5"><span lang="EN-US"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">The Minimum and Maximum values were defined in the range section of Inspection pane.</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Minimum</font></span></b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">- the lower zero range border</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Maximum</font></span></b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">- the upper zero range border</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Inside</font></span></b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">- the percentage of points inside the zero range</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Outside</font></span></b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">- the percentage of points outside the zero range</font></span></p>
<p class="whs5"><span lang="EN-US"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">In the table on the bottom of the dialogue, you can see what percentage of the points enter the</font></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>1xSigma</b></span><span lang="EN-US">,</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>2xSigma</b></span><span lang="EN-US">,</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>3xSigma</b></span><span lang="EN-US">... &#160;interval. Usually about 95% of the points enter the</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>2xSigma</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">interval.</span></p>
